[[:db/add "dd86225b-0360-5369-b818-734884e1d85f" :answer/id #uuid "dd86225b-0360-5369-b818-734884e1d85f"] [:db/add "dd86225b-0360-5369-b818-734884e1d85f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "dd86225b-0360-5369-b818-734884e1d85f" :answer/value "-1"] [:db/ensure "dd86225b-0360-5369-b818-734884e1d85f" :answer/validate] [:db/add "ad0b66e3-80be-5103-8c94-63d5a847a379" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad0b66e3-80be-5103-8c94-63d5a847a379"] [:db/add "ad0b66e3-80be-5103-8c94-63d5a847a379" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "ad0b66e3-80be-5103-8c94-63d5a847a379" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "ad0b66e3-80be-5103-8c94-63d5a847a379" :answer-field/choices "dd86225b-0360-5369-b818-734884e1d85f"] [:db/add "ad0b66e3-80be-5103-8c94-63d5a847a379" :answer-field/correct "dd86225b-0360-5369-b818-734884e1d85f"] [:db/ensure "ad0b66e3-80be-5103-8c94-63d5a847a379" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "e5e9d9ef-4bff-5ec3-8248-1e14edc7489e" :question/id #uuid "e5e9d9ef-4bff-5ec3-8248-1e14edc7489e"] [:db/add "e5e9d9ef-4bff-5ec3-8248-1e14edc7489e" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/c5/c5005b41d3043021e1578181865fbbff202dbd374ad4c5c7a612119c84c50e7a.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "e5e9d9ef-4bff-5ec3-8248-1e14edc7489e" :question/worked-solution "First trace $-3\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: reverse its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/01/012ff6ccf1a14477bb728f501e08c8062ac30f3fafe4c875374c86123a0299fa.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $2$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{2}{2}=1$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=-3\\mathbf{b}+(-\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "e5e9d9ef-4bff-5ec3-8248-1e14edc7489e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "e5e9d9ef-4bff-5ec3-8248-1e14edc7489e" :question/answer-fields "ad0b66e3-80be-5103-8c94-63d5a847a379"] [:db/ensure "e5e9d9ef-4bff-5ec3-8248-1e14edc7489e" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "e5e9d9ef-4bff-5ec3-8248-1e14edc7489e"] [:db/add "eb1ff109-5171-5ae4-b5a2-1fdd719da959" :answer/id #uuid "eb1ff109-5171-5ae4-b5a2-1fdd719da959"] [:db/add "eb1ff109-5171-5ae4-b5a2-1fdd719da959" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "eb1ff109-5171-5ae4-b5a2-1fdd719da959" :answer/value "-7"] [:db/ensure "eb1ff109-5171-5ae4-b5a2-1fdd719da959" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e14b7216-d38f-589e-a731-a96a32ea2560" :answer/id #uuid "e14b7216-d38f-589e-a731-a96a32ea2560"] [:db/add "e14b7216-d38f-589e-a731-a96a32ea2560" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e14b7216-d38f-589e-a731-a96a32ea2560" :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}"] [:db/ensure "e14b7216-d38f-589e-a731-a96a32ea2560" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f836cdc9-1939-5f4c-ae06-42f076ca0705" :answer/id #uuid "f836cdc9-1939-5f4c-ae06-42f076ca0705"] [:db/add "f836cdc9-1939-5f4c-ae06-42f076ca0705" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "f836cdc9-1939-5f4c-ae06-42f076ca0705" :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}"] [:db/ensure "f836cdc9-1939-5f4c-ae06-42f076ca0705" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f93daf1e-abb5-5781-96a6-2b36effea11a" :answer/id #uuid "f93daf1e-abb5-5781-96a6-2b36effea11a"] [:db/add "f93daf1e-abb5-5781-96a6-2b36effea11a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "f93daf1e-abb5-5781-96a6-2b36effea11a" :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}"] [:db/ensure "f93daf1e-abb5-5781-96a6-2b36effea11a" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f525cc52-199b-51c4-8ad3-0756db2d62a0" :answer/id #uuid "f525cc52-199b-51c4-8ad3-0756db2d62a0"] [:db/add "f525cc52-199b-51c4-8ad3-0756db2d62a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "f525cc52-199b-51c4-8ad3-0756db2d62a0" :answer/value "-3"] [:db/ensure "f525cc52-199b-51c4-8ad3-0756db2d62a0" :answer/validate] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374"] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/choices "eb1ff109-5171-5ae4-b5a2-1fdd719da959"] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/choices "e14b7216-d38f-589e-a731-a96a32ea2560"] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/choices "f836cdc9-1939-5f4c-ae06-42f076ca0705"] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/choices "f93daf1e-abb5-5781-96a6-2b36effea11a"] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/choices "f525cc52-199b-51c4-8ad3-0756db2d62a0"] [:db/add "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/correct "f836cdc9-1939-5f4c-ae06-42f076ca0705"] [:db/ensure "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "a70c1342-2d28-5547-9387-d9366f97c9fc" :question/id #uuid "a70c1342-2d28-5547-9387-d9366f97c9fc"] [:db/add "a70c1342-2d28-5547-9387-d9366f97c9fc" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/4d/4df626a8261fd3c1bb508427c81cae685ff53f1cb88d7b46ccd510289f8c879e.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "a70c1342-2d28-5547-9387-d9366f97c9fc" :question/worked-solution "First trace $-4\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: reverse its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/d2/d29b30270bcaf446c5e2c142bc081865ace2e3edec00ad9030a443ae8a071abd.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $7$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{7}{2}=\\frac{7}{2}$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=-4\\mathbf{b}+\\left(-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{7}{2}$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "a70c1342-2d28-5547-9387-d9366f97c9fc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "a70c1342-2d28-5547-9387-d9366f97c9fc" :question/answer-fields "4d3a7dfd-60aa-5b7f-8b26-3e8571dc6374"] [:db/ensure "a70c1342-2d28-5547-9387-d9366f97c9fc" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "a70c1342-2d28-5547-9387-d9366f97c9fc"] [:db/add "7cd2e45e-b269-5a56-b103-d9f2eefe0cca" :answer/id #uuid "7cd2e45e-b269-5a56-b103-d9f2eefe0cca"] [:db/add "7cd2e45e-b269-5a56-b103-d9f2eefe0cca" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "7cd2e45e-b269-5a56-b103-d9f2eefe0cca" :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}"] [:db/ensure "7cd2e45e-b269-5a56-b103-d9f2eefe0cca" :answer/validate] [:db/add "7b704d93-ae1b-58ff-ab6b-7855b760e13b" :answer/id #uuid "7b704d93-ae1b-58ff-ab6b-7855b760e13b"] [:db/add "7b704d93-ae1b-58ff-ab6b-7855b760e13b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "7b704d93-ae1b-58ff-ab6b-7855b760e13b" :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}"] [:db/ensure "7b704d93-ae1b-58ff-ab6b-7855b760e13b" :answer/validate] [:db/add "fcfdaf0e-d69f-59ad-90f9-d0cf9613976c" :answer/id #uuid "fcfdaf0e-d69f-59ad-90f9-d0cf9613976c"] [:db/add "fcfdaf0e-d69f-59ad-90f9-d0cf9613976c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "fcfdaf0e-d69f-59ad-90f9-d0cf9613976c" :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}"] [:db/ensure "fcfdaf0e-d69f-59ad-90f9-d0cf9613976c" :answer/validate] [:db/add "9041a2cf-1c21-5fb8-b70e-1eeb343dd913" :answer/id #uuid "9041a2cf-1c21-5fb8-b70e-1eeb343dd913"] [:db/add "9041a2cf-1c21-5fb8-b70e-1eeb343dd913" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "9041a2cf-1c21-5fb8-b70e-1eeb343dd913" :answer/value "-3"] [:db/ensure "9041a2cf-1c21-5fb8-b70e-1eeb343dd913" :answer/validate] [:db/add "baef78c0-6977-598c-b343-e2b531ed9302" :answer/id #uuid "baef78c0-6977-598c-b343-e2b531ed9302"] [:db/add "baef78c0-6977-598c-b343-e2b531ed9302" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "baef78c0-6977-598c-b343-e2b531ed9302" :answer/value "-1"] [:db/ensure "baef78c0-6977-598c-b343-e2b531ed9302" :answer/validate] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d"] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/choices "7cd2e45e-b269-5a56-b103-d9f2eefe0cca"] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/choices "7b704d93-ae1b-58ff-ab6b-7855b760e13b"] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/choices "fcfdaf0e-d69f-59ad-90f9-d0cf9613976c"] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/choices "9041a2cf-1c21-5fb8-b70e-1eeb343dd913"] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/choices "baef78c0-6977-598c-b343-e2b531ed9302"] [:db/add "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/correct "baef78c0-6977-598c-b343-e2b531ed9302"] [:db/ensure "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "60bed3d7-87d0-585c-a69a-78b3e9347c0f" :question/id #uuid "60bed3d7-87d0-585c-a69a-78b3e9347c0f"] [:db/add "60bed3d7-87d0-585c-a69a-78b3e9347c0f" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/01/016049db389747b5de548d97dbb7501dee2d0a4c0c3f0d28ada38ff5bde37965.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "60bed3d7-87d0-585c-a69a-78b3e9347c0f" :question/worked-solution "First trace $-4\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: reverse its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/42/42ffed80805b7281c04b6be0aa10ea5a56ea1ecb831ecbf14a4053c7b3b5545f.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $3$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $3$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{3}{3}=1$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=-4\\mathbf{b}+(-\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "60bed3d7-87d0-585c-a69a-78b3e9347c0f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "60bed3d7-87d0-585c-a69a-78b3e9347c0f" :question/answer-fields "fc83db0d-7987-548f-a8b2-d09f58d77b9d"] [:db/ensure "60bed3d7-87d0-585c-a69a-78b3e9347c0f" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "60bed3d7-87d0-585c-a69a-78b3e9347c0f"] [:db/add "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc" :answer/id #uuid "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc"] [:db/add "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc" :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}"] [:db/ensure "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc" :answer/validate] [:db/add "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9" :answer-field/id #uuid "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9"] [:db/add "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9" :answer-field/choices "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc"] [:db/add "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9" :answer-field/correct "b303d4d3-ce5c-579b-a1b0-62fcabce16dc"] [:db/ensure "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955" :question/id #uuid "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955"] [:db/add "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/b4/b4062187cb72ba000d61cc7c906acda03eb38b8f34bd752344904fdeca809e10.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955" :question/worked-solution "First trace $-\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: reverse its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/a5/a51afe201aca53375a46ff439b03e2b3f8fec058fb06871aa1398d9dc7e4ebef.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $7$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{7}{2}=\\frac{7}{2}$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{b}+\\left(-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{7}{2}$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955" :question/answer-fields "99d07ee7-8006-57cf-b92d-1ca61d0ec6c9"] [:db/ensure "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "6186f711-696a-5694-91f1-4323d8641955"] [:db/add "53903e91-264c-5950-8720-3c35a1f5535a" :answer/id #uuid "53903e91-264c-5950-8720-3c35a1f5535a"] [:db/add "53903e91-264c-5950-8720-3c35a1f5535a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "53903e91-264c-5950-8720-3c35a1f5535a" :answer/value "-2"] [:db/ensure "53903e91-264c-5950-8720-3c35a1f5535a" :answer/validate] [:db/add "0d2289c1-e208-571a-88ed-ed71dabaea58" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d2289c1-e208-571a-88ed-ed71dabaea58"] [:db/add "0d2289c1-e208-571a-88ed-ed71dabaea58" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "0d2289c1-e208-571a-88ed-ed71dabaea58" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "0d2289c1-e208-571a-88ed-ed71dabaea58" :answer-field/choices "53903e91-264c-5950-8720-3c35a1f5535a"] [:db/add "0d2289c1-e208-571a-88ed-ed71dabaea58" :answer-field/correct "53903e91-264c-5950-8720-3c35a1f5535a"] [:db/ensure "0d2289c1-e208-571a-88ed-ed71dabaea58" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "94b16251-3b94-5363-9ff7-99e4b50db4f3" :question/id #uuid "94b16251-3b94-5363-9ff7-99e4b50db4f3"] [:db/add "94b16251-3b94-5363-9ff7-99e4b50db4f3" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/df/df667def06d7d97e84c530bcaca31434e3b5f4473bca9924338eb18a3629d1bf.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "94b16251-3b94-5363-9ff7-99e4b50db4f3" :question/worked-solution "First trace $-4\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: reverse its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/bd/bd4ab331771afde18721332299a5bf1422167f5329c306247eb26890baa0312e.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $3$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $6$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{6}{3}=2$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-2\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=-4\\mathbf{b}+(-2\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-2\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-4\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-2$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "94b16251-3b94-5363-9ff7-99e4b50db4f3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "94b16251-3b94-5363-9ff7-99e4b50db4f3" :question/answer-fields "0d2289c1-e208-571a-88ed-ed71dabaea58"] [:db/ensure "94b16251-3b94-5363-9ff7-99e4b50db4f3" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "94b16251-3b94-5363-9ff7-99e4b50db4f3"] [:db/add "b1970014-dea0-5dc5-8055-252ef73b61aa" :answer/id #uuid "b1970014-dea0-5dc5-8055-252ef73b61aa"] [:db/add "b1970014-dea0-5dc5-8055-252ef73b61aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "b1970014-dea0-5dc5-8055-252ef73b61aa" :answer/value "-\\frac{14}{5}"] [:db/ensure "b1970014-dea0-5dc5-8055-252ef73b61aa" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e9d5e5b1-fb61-5934-bfc7-df1e8a80d993" :answer/id #uuid "e9d5e5b1-fb61-5934-bfc7-df1e8a80d993"] [:db/add "e9d5e5b1-fb61-5934-bfc7-df1e8a80d993" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e9d5e5b1-fb61-5934-bfc7-df1e8a80d993" :answer/value "-\\frac{14}{3}"] [:db/ensure "e9d5e5b1-fb61-5934-bfc7-df1e8a80d993" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e0c3e4c8-6d47-5a08-b14a-5029b91f9747" :answer/id #uuid "e0c3e4c8-6d47-5a08-b14a-5029b91f9747"] [:db/add "e0c3e4c8-6d47-5a08-b14a-5029b91f9747" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e0c3e4c8-6d47-5a08-b14a-5029b91f9747" :answer/value "-14"] [:db/ensure "e0c3e4c8-6d47-5a08-b14a-5029b91f9747" :answer/validate] [:db/add "0c668f57-27f4-58f5-a1d4-49f8becc32f0" :answer/id #uuid "0c668f57-27f4-58f5-a1d4-49f8becc32f0"] [:db/add "0c668f57-27f4-58f5-a1d4-49f8becc32f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "0c668f57-27f4-58f5-a1d4-49f8becc32f0" :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}"] [:db/ensure "0c668f57-27f4-58f5-a1d4-49f8becc32f0" :answer/validate] [:db/add "3e024643-c01a-51dd-a87f-d5e656395ab2" :answer/id #uuid "3e024643-c01a-51dd-a87f-d5e656395ab2"] [:db/add "3e024643-c01a-51dd-a87f-d5e656395ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "3e024643-c01a-51dd-a87f-d5e656395ab2" :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{4}"] [:db/ensure "3e024643-c01a-51dd-a87f-d5e656395ab2" :answer/validate] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/id #uuid "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a"] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/choices "b1970014-dea0-5dc5-8055-252ef73b61aa"] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/choices "e9d5e5b1-fb61-5934-bfc7-df1e8a80d993"] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/choices "e0c3e4c8-6d47-5a08-b14a-5029b91f9747"] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/choices "0c668f57-27f4-58f5-a1d4-49f8becc32f0"] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/choices "3e024643-c01a-51dd-a87f-d5e656395ab2"] [:db/add "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/correct "0c668f57-27f4-58f5-a1d4-49f8becc32f0"] [:db/ensure "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "4d319e55-4ce6-50c0-9e3a-4d9f51ec4a2f" :question/id #uuid "4d319e55-4ce6-50c0-9e3a-4d9f51ec4a2f"] [:db/add "4d319e55-4ce6-50c0-9e3a-4d9f51ec4a2f" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/8a/8ae6de61a081cac653838785257729f75a337347c685d8e89eae4b6ec4e1d91d.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "4d319e55-4ce6-50c0-9e3a-4d9f51ec4a2f" :question/worked-solution "First trace $-2\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: reverse its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/db/db3e4e3ec71dbdbfef033f9f669cfb67e4bc4f4ad3d07688e37daa277b317ddc.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $4$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $14$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{14}{4}=\\frac{7}{2}$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=-2\\mathbf{b}+\\left(-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{7}{2}\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{7}{2}$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "4d319e55-4ce6-50c0-9e3a-4d9f51ec4a2f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "4d319e55-4ce6-50c0-9e3a-4d9f51ec4a2f" :question/answer-fields "145acafb-4493-5532-a1fa-259523bf846a"] [:db/ensure "4d319e55-4ce6-50c0-9e3a-4d9f51ec4a2f" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "4d31